                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/>
              </svg>
            </summary>
            <div class="p-4 text-stone-700 leading-relaxed">
              Yes — Rhode Island's low-elevation trails stay hikeable through most of the winter with basic traction, though ice is
              common after freeze-thaw cycles. For the higher day-trip destinations like Mount Monadnock, microspikes or crampons
              and full winter layers are essential.
            </div>
          </details>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Hiking Tips for Providence Area -->
      <section class="bg-gradient-to-br from-emerald-50 to-blue-50 rounded-2xl p-8 border border-emerald-200">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mb-6">Essential Tips for Hiking Near Providence</h2>

        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
              <span class="text-2xl">🚗</span> Getting There
            </h3>
            <ul class="space-y-2 text-stone-700">
              <li>• RI's own trail cluster is reachable via I-295 and RI-6 in under 30 minutes</li>
              <li>• For Connecticut ridgelines, take I-95 W or CT-14</li>
              <li>• For Mount Monadnock, take I-95 N to Route 12A</li>
              <li>• Download offline maps in case of poor cell service on back roads</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
              <span class="text-2xl">🎒</span> What to Bring
            </h3>
            <ul class="space-y-2 text-stone-700">
              <li>• Water: 2+ liters per person</li>
              <li>• Snacks: Trail mix, energy bars, fruit</li>
              <li>• Layers: New England weather shifts fast</li>
              <li>• First aid kit & headlamp</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
              <span class="text-2xl">📅</span> Best Times to Visit
            </h3>
            <ul class="space-y-2 text-stone-700">
              <li>• <strong>Summer (Jun-Aug):</strong> Best weather, most crowded</li>
              <li>• <strong>Fall (Sep-Oct):</strong> Peak New England foliage</li>
              <li>• <strong>Spring (Apr-May):</strong> Mud season on wooded trails</li>
              <li>• <strong>Winter (Dec-Mar):</strong> RI hills stay walkable; day-trip peaks need traction</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
              <span class="text-2xl">⚠️</span> Safety First
            </h3>
